cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Hypervisor-Free Windows on Apple Silicon: The AIC Problem"
abstract: >-
  A research concept and reproducibility plan for investigating whether Windows
  11 ARM64 can boot on Apple Silicon without an EL2 hypervisor shim by teaching
  the Windows HAL to drive Apple's AIC interrupt controller. Includes a prior-art
  survey, an upstream code survey, a staged roadmap, and a QEMU-based validation
  strategy.
authors:
  - name: "xorica27"
date-released: "2026-10-21"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Apple Silicon
  - Windows on ARM
  - AIC
  - interrupt controller
  - QEMU
  - reverse engineering
  - hypervisor
  - UEFI
  - ACPI
  - Asahi Linux
